# Project-specific commit scopes for scoped-commits.sh (one per line; # = comment).
#
# The hook already accepts, automatically: every spec/feature `id:` in Specs/ &
# features/, each features/<slug>, the harness areas (hooks, skills, commands,
# agents, templates, rules, docs, mise, readme), plus `specs` and `treewide`.
# List here only the scopes that aren't derivable that way.
#
# This is a single Swift library (Sources/ + Tests/), so there are no apps/ or
# services/ scopes. A behavior change should be scoped to its spec/feature `id:`;
# the scopes below cover the non-spec parts of the package.
swift      # library implementation not bound to a single spec id
package    # Package.swift / Package.resolved / SPM manifest
tests      # test-only changes not bound to a single spec id
tooling    # formatter / linter config (dprint, swift-format, .vscode)
